WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.810
Resgrid Relay listens to an audio feed, detects configured tones, records dispatch audio,

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:11.620
and creates calls for the associated department or groups. It can help departments

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:17.430
connect an existing paging process when they cannot modify the upstream dispatch system.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:23.617
The recording plan begins with an approved sample audio feed and known tone

00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:29.204
frequencies. Check the input signal, configure the intended recording behavior, and review the

00:00:29.204 --> 00:00:34.791
department or group recipients. Verify the exact installer and interface against the supported

00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:36.510
Relay release before capture.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.985
Use synthetic test audio. Inspect the resulting call, the captured recording, and the

00:00:42.985 --> 00:00:48.861
intended recipients. Test nonmatching tones separately and document what was observed. The public

00:00:48.861 --> 00:00:54.736
Relay installation page contains incomplete older steps, so it is a feature reference

00:00:54.736 --> 00:00:57.900
rather than a verified modern installation procedure.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.029
Retain the synthetic audio fixture, selected release, approved configuration, and observed test result.

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:09.558
A recorder will need the supported Relay application and an audio test setup

00:01:09.558 --> 00:01:12.960
to turn this briefing into a live walkthrough.

